   "type": "text",
   "text": "✗ **H2035_L5_m2_z4_syndrome_and_r48_khatri_rao** · hypothesis\n\nM2 Representation Pivot: (1) Exact F_2-linear Z_4 Hensel syndrome solver J_S * y = r_2(S) (mod 2) guiding flip/plus-transition walks directly from rank-47 F_2 schemes (alphatensor_F2, flips_mod2) toward Z_4 liftability (p2), and (2) G_16/G_8-equivariant Khatri-Rao lattice saturation & 3-collinear plus-transition search from rank-49 Z schemes toward rank-48 Z (p1).\n\n*why dead:* [L-F4R3-006=0] Proved Theorem 7 (Z_4 Cokernel Invariance under F_2 Flips: Delta r_2 = u1 x (v1^v2) x w1 + u1 x v2 x (w1 + w1^w2) lies in im_F2(J_S) cap im_F2(J_S')) and proved both alphatensor_F2 and flips_mod2 are isolated (0 direct flips) and infinitesimally rigid over F_2 (rank_F2(J_S) = 2117 = 2256 - 139); across 6,536 schemes in guided_z4_hunter.cpp, coker_wt hits a floor of 11 at R=47 and 6 at R=48 because Theorem 7 traps the local F_2 flip basin in a non-zero Z_4-syndrome coset.",
